new Paine Field airframes are often untyped) are counted as 'unknown program'. They are real first flights and deliveries, shown separately, and are not part of any program's 737, 767, 777 or 777X count.","Boeing's own flight-test fleet (for example N779X*, N2775x, N836BA, and typed Boeing-owned jets) is excluded from production counts.","Program comes from the birth field and ICAO type code: Renton is 737; Paine Field jets use their type code, else 'unknown'. 737 MAX 10s at Paine Field are read as 737 because the 737 North Line in Everett began low-rate production in July 2026.","Deliveries seen are departures from a Boeing field under a non-BOE callsign with no return in the history. They are a sky estimate, not Boeing's delivery count.","Reported deliveries are Boeing's monthly figures as relayed by Forecast International, checked against Boeing's quarterly releases. Boeing's 737 count includes the 737-800A (the P-8 airframe); its 767 count includes the KC-46 airframe.","Receiver coverage is uneven and the scanner drops days it cannot read. Missing days are listed in coverage and the sky count is a floor, not a census."]}
